WEBVTT

00:12.400 --> 00:15.710
Oh, yeah. I am a finely tuned machine.

00:20.920 --> 00:23.195
- Hello.
- Are you a friend of Charlie's?

00:23.360 --> 00:24.679
I'm his brother.

00:24.840 --> 00:26.319
So, no.

00:27.360 --> 00:29.874
- I'm Gabrielle.
- Nice to meet you.

00:30.240 --> 00:31.468
I'm Alan.

00:31.640 --> 00:35.155
Or, as you would say, "Alan."

00:35.320 --> 00:37.117
Why would I say that?

00:37.520 --> 00:39.715
No reason. I'm a little dehydrated.

00:40.880 --> 00:43.792
- So you are a cyclist.
- A what?

00:44.520 --> 00:47.318
A cyclist? You know, with your bicycle.

00:48.640 --> 00:51.518
Yes, yes. I'm very passionate about...

00:52.440 --> 00:53.873
..."bicycling."

00:55.160 --> 00:58.835
I even have a stationary "cycle."

01:01.240 --> 01:03.674
I also jog and ab-crunch...

01:03.840 --> 01:08.516
...and, of course, &lt;i>les&lt;/i> buns of steel.

01:18.680 --> 01:22.036
- Nice, huh?
- Nice? She's magnificent.

01:22.200 --> 01:25.476
- You should see her naked.
- Can I?

01:26.600 --> 01:28.352
Well, I could show you some pictures...

01:28.520 --> 01:30.556
...but you may not wanna see
that much of me.

01:32.160 --> 01:35.550
Just out of curiosity,
where do you find women like that?

01:35.720 --> 01:39.156
And, more importantly, how do you
get them to go to bed with you?

01:39.480 --> 01:42.790
- You really wanna know?
- Yeah. What's your secret?

01:42.960 --> 01:47.272
Well, you see, Alan, it's like this:

01:50.000 --> 01:51.797
I got a knack.

01:53.920 --> 01:57.549
- That's not a secret.
- Well, I didn't think so, but you asked.

01:58.000 --> 02:01.879
- So that's it? You've got a knack?
- Hey, everybody's good at something.

02:02.040 --> 02:03.519
You, for instance...

02:07.560 --> 02:08.629
...have no shame.

02:10.080 --> 02:12.913
Excuse me, this is what they wear
in the Tour de France.

02:13.680 --> 02:16.592
Alan, I just took a Tour de France.

02:19.480 --> 02:22.040
And the only thing I was wearing
was a smile and a condom.

02:35.680 --> 02:38.240
- Hi, Judith. Hey, buddy.
- Hey.

02:38.720 --> 02:40.233
What's the matter with him?

02:40.400 --> 02:42.834
- His little girlfriend broke up with him.
- Oh, no.

02:43.000 --> 02:45.992
Yeah. I was hoping you could
talk to him, because, let's face it...

02:46.160 --> 02:47.991
...who knows more
about getting dumped?

02:51.040 --> 02:53.474
- Don't flatter me, Judith. I'll talk to him.
- I'm sorry.

02:53.640 --> 02:56.791
- That didn't come out the way I meant it.
- Really? How did you mean it?

02:56.960 --> 02:59.428
Couldn't you just take the "I'm sorry"?

03:00.200 --> 03:03.829
Couldn't you have just loved me?

03:06.480 --> 03:08.835
- Did I hear Numbnuts come in?
- Numbnuts?

03:09.000 --> 03:10.752
Sorry. Numbnuts Jr.

03:11.920 --> 03:15.230
- Lf you mean my son, yes, he's here.
- Crap.

03:18.480 --> 03:20.914
- What are you doing?
- Hiding my cookies.

03:21.720 --> 03:23.597
- Why?
- Because I just bought a new bag...

03:23.760 --> 03:26.399
...and I don't want that knucklehead
to eat them all.

03:26.680 --> 03:29.752
Oh, Charlie. You hide your cookies
from a little boy who loves you?

03:29.920 --> 03:32.593
"Little boy," my ass.
He's a bottomless pit.

03:32.760 --> 03:36.958
And I'm tired of going for a snack and
having to lick cookie dust out of the bag.

03:37.280 --> 03:38.872
You might wanna take it easy on him.

03:39.040 --> 03:40.758
- He's going through a breakup.
- Really?

03:40.920 --> 03:41.955
Yeah.

03:54.560 --> 03:56.471
Nope. My cookies.

04:02.400 --> 04:06.678
- So how was school this week?
- Okay.

04:07.080 --> 04:10.038
- Anything noteworthy happen?
- No.

04:11.200 --> 04:12.599
Thought you said he got dumped.

04:20.640 --> 04:24.519
- I was easing into it.
- Oh, good idea. Go ahead.

04:25.800 --> 04:28.109
Jake, sooner or later,
every guy gets dumped.

04:28.760 --> 04:31.593
Some guys get dumped sooner and later,
right, Alan?

04:33.560 --> 04:35.710
Sorry. I should've eased into that.

04:37.120 --> 04:39.554
My point is, you've got nothing
to be embarrassed about.

04:39.720 --> 04:42.393
I'm not embarrassed. I'm angry.
She didn't even tell me why.

04:42.560 --> 04:45.836
She just sent me an e-mail saying she
doesn't wanna go out with me anymore.

04:46.000 --> 04:47.399
Maybe she found somebody better.

04:47.560 --> 04:50.438
What do you mean, better?
Who's better than Jake?

04:52.800 --> 04:54.518
Why, no one, Alan.

04:56.040 --> 04:58.679
He's the pinnacle of male evolution.

04:59.640 --> 05:00.629
Thank you.

05:02.880 --> 05:04.677
Look, buddy,
I know exactly how you feel.

05:04.840 --> 05:07.070
When I was your age,
I was dating a beautiful girl:

05:07.240 --> 05:10.550
Charity Kirschenbaum.
I was crazy about her.

05:10.720 --> 05:13.837
Then, the night before junior prom,
she called and dumped me.

05:14.000 --> 05:16.195
Wouldn't even give me a reason.
I was devastated.

05:16.360 --> 05:18.874
- So, what'd you do?
- What could I do?

05:19.040 --> 05:20.598
How can you mend a broken heart?

05:20.760 --> 05:24.150
&lt;i>How can you stop the rain&lt;/i>
&lt;i>From falling down?&lt;/i>

05:28.160 --> 05:31.550
- You done?
- Unless you wanna hear "Jive Talkin'."

05:35.520 --> 05:36.748
The thing is, Jake...

05:36.920 --> 05:40.071
...that no matter how bad you feel now,
eventually, it'll pass.

05:40.240 --> 05:42.595
You just have to be willing
to live with the pain.

05:42.760 --> 05:44.716
- No, he doesn't.
- Yes, he does.

05:44.880 --> 05:47.189
Hang on, Dad.
What do you mean, no, I don't?

05:47.360 --> 05:50.238
When you get dumped, don't
sit around feeling sorry for yourself.

05:50.400 --> 05:52.994
You go out and find another girl,
a better girl.

05:53.480 --> 05:55.357
Okay, but how am I
gonna get another girl?

05:55.520 --> 05:57.590
I don't know how I got this one.

05:57.760 --> 05:59.512
You don't know
how you got a girlfriend?

05:59.680 --> 06:01.159
No, it just kind of happened.

06:01.320 --> 06:02.594
Yeah, I know how that goes.

06:04.240 --> 06:07.869
Wake up in the morning, and there
she is. Shut up. I know that was wrong.

06:09.080 --> 06:12.197
Look, Jake,
who is the cutest girl in your class?

06:12.360 --> 06:14.635
- Nicole O'Malley.
- Okay, call Nicole O'Malley...

06:14.800 --> 06:17.189
...and ask her out.
- You drunk?

06:17.680 --> 06:19.238
A little.

06:21.440 --> 06:26.150
But this is a secret that will
serve you for the rest of your life:

06:26.320 --> 06:28.356
The hotter the girl, the Ionelier she is...

06:28.520 --> 06:30.750
...because most guys
are too scared to talk to her.

06:30.920 --> 06:32.353
- Really?
- Really?

06:32.920 --> 06:34.751
Trust me.

06:37.440 --> 06:39.670
Why couldn't you have said this
20 years ago?

06:39.840 --> 06:42.559
Come on, Dad.
I wasn't even born 20 years ago.

06:43.040 --> 06:46.749
I really shouldn't be giving him advice
that could help him reproduce, should I?

07:01.440 --> 07:03.874
Oh, it's just you.

07:04.040 --> 07:05.678
Hey.

07:07.680 --> 07:08.954
What are you doing?

07:09.120 --> 07:14.990
I am drinking some of your finest Scotch
and looking at my high-school yearbook.

07:15.640 --> 07:17.596
Charity Kirschenbaum.

07:17.760 --> 07:21.150
I can't help wondering
how my life would've turned out...

07:21.320 --> 07:23.197
...if she hadn't dumped me.

07:23.360 --> 07:25.078
Come on, your life turned out great.

07:27.840 --> 07:30.195
Well, it wouldn't have turned out
any better.

07:30.560 --> 07:31.913
You know what?

07:32.080 --> 07:36.198
I'm gonna call her
and find out why she broke my heart.

07:36.360 --> 07:37.429
Good thinking.

07:37.600 --> 07:40.319
Call your high-school girlfriend drunk
at 2 in the morning.

07:40.480 --> 07:44.473
While you're at it, why don't you expose
yourself to an undercover policewoman?

07:44.880 --> 07:46.791
Some people do that.

07:47.160 --> 07:51.073
I need closure. I need to understand
why she dumped me.

07:52.840 --> 07:53.989
What's to understand?

07:56.640 --> 07:58.358
This is her.

07:59.880 --> 08:01.154
This is you.

08:03.000 --> 08:05.355
Peaches-and-cream complexion.

08:05.960 --> 08:07.313
You.

08:08.720 --> 08:10.472
Cheerleader.

08:10.720 --> 08:11.709
You.

08:13.600 --> 08:15.318
Stop me any time.

08:15.480 --> 08:18.677
I don't care. I got her number
off the Internet, and I'm calling her.

08:18.840 --> 08:20.398
Oh, man.

08:20.560 --> 08:23.393
When are they gonna invent a phone
with a Breathalyzer lock?

08:24.000 --> 08:25.592
It's ringing.

08:26.440 --> 08:27.714
Hello?

08:27.880 --> 08:29.711
Hello? Is this Charity?

08:31.200 --> 08:33.714
Hi, Charity. This is Alan Harper.

08:34.480 --> 08:36.948
Yeah, yeah, from high school.

08:37.120 --> 08:38.838
Anyway...

08:39.760 --> 08:41.796
Yeah, I know it's late.

08:42.080 --> 08:44.116
Yeah, I know I'm drunk.

08:44.280 --> 08:47.397
Listen, I just need to ask you
one question.

08:47.840 --> 08:50.434
Why did you dump me
on the night before junior prom?

08:55.120 --> 08:57.190
Okay. Okay.

08:57.360 --> 09:00.158
Okay, thanks. Go back to sleep.

09:01.680 --> 09:05.878
She said, to ask my brother, Cha...

09:08.840 --> 09:10.558
- rlie.

09:20.880 --> 09:22.677
Oh, that's why.

09:32.640 --> 09:33.789
Morning.

09:33.960 --> 09:35.439
Morning.

09:39.240 --> 09:40.673
You found the stash, huh?

09:41.000 --> 09:42.399
Wasn't well-hidden.

09:42.560 --> 09:44.710
Okay, just for the record,
that stuff's medicinal.

09:44.880 --> 09:46.552
I've got glaucoma.

09:47.720 --> 09:50.234
- What are you talking about?
- Nothing.

09:54.480 --> 09:56.391
- Morning.
- Morning.

09:56.800 --> 09:59.268
- So where'd you disappear to last night?
- Me?

09:59.440 --> 10:00.998
I decided to take a little drive...

10:01.160 --> 10:04.311
...give you a chance to calm down
about Charity Kirschenbaum.

10:04.880 --> 10:06.598
- I'm perfectly calm.
- Good.

10:06.760 --> 10:08.910
Who's Charity Kirschenbaum?

10:09.080 --> 10:12.516
It's just a little thing that's
not worth getting upset about, and...

10:12.680 --> 10:15.035
Hey, what the hell are you doing
with my cookies?

10:15.560 --> 10:17.755
- They're yours?
- You know they're mine.

10:17.920 --> 10:23.392
Oh, so you're saying I took something
that belonged to you, and you're upset?

10:27.880 --> 10:29.279
Oh, come on, Alan.

10:29.840 --> 10:33.150
I loved Charity Kirschenbaum, and
you stole her right out from under me.

10:33.360 --> 10:35.794
He's speaking metaphorically, right?

10:36.680 --> 10:38.591
Yeah. He was never on top of that.

10:40.200 --> 10:45.320
- I would've been, if it weren't for you.
- Okay, fine. I took your girl 20 years ago.

10:45.480 --> 10:49.473
That calls for maybe five, six cookies,
tops, not the whole damn bag.

10:49.640 --> 10:51.870
I had to go to junior prom
with cousin Phoebe.

10:52.560 --> 10:55.597
- She was cute.
- She was 12 and in a body cast.

10:55.760 --> 10:57.591
Well, so what? She was your cousin.

10:57.760 --> 10:59.910
She could've been 18
and in a cellophane bikini...

11:00.080 --> 11:02.071
...and you weren't gonna get any.

11:02.880 --> 11:06.111
You are a horrible human being,
and I hope you burn in hell.

11:07.760 --> 11:11.878
- So we're good?
- No! We're not good!

11:12.040 --> 11:14.270
We suck!

11:15.960 --> 11:18.235
- Freshen that up for you?
- Thanks.

11:18.400 --> 11:21.949
You betrayed me!

11:22.280 --> 11:25.670
I hate you!

11:25.960 --> 11:28.952
I hate you! I hate you!

11:29.120 --> 11:32.954
I hate you!

11:34.120 --> 11:36.588
Sounds like he's going for a bike ride.

11:39.760 --> 11:41.830
Hello? Nicole O'Malley?

11:42.000 --> 11:43.513
Jake Harper here.

11:43.680 --> 11:47.309
Harper. I sit next to you
in geometry class.

11:47.480 --> 11:48.993
No, the other side.

11:49.160 --> 11:50.718
Yeah, with the big head.

11:52.760 --> 11:55.797
I was wondering if you would go
to the winter dance with me.

11:56.400 --> 11:59.437
Really? Are you sure?

11:59.600 --> 12:03.593
Well, great.
I guess I'll see you at school. Bye.

12:04.480 --> 12:07.517
- Uncle Charlie's a genius.
- In a sense.

12:08.360 --> 12:11.352
But there's book smart and "look smart."

12:14.400 --> 12:16.675
- Would you get that, Berta?
- What?

12:16.840 --> 12:19.957
- The door.
- I can't hear you.

12:20.120 --> 12:23.510
- I said, would you get the door?
- I can't. I'm upstairs.

12:29.400 --> 12:31.197
Hi, Judith. Jake, your mom's here.

12:31.720 --> 12:33.756
- Did you talk to him?
- I did.

12:33.920 --> 12:35.751
- Hey, Mom.
- Hey, honey. How's it going?

12:35.920 --> 12:39.754
- Great. Uncle Charlie's a genius.
- Good, good.

12:40.120 --> 12:42.076
- You said you talked to him.
- I did.

12:42.240 --> 12:45.755
- Then why is Uncle Charlie a genius?
- Because he never got married.

12:48.920 --> 12:52.196
Oh, that's gonna come back
to bite me in the ass.

12:54.440 --> 12:57.796
And here it comes, jaws a-snapping.

12:58.840 --> 13:01.274
All right, I'm sorry.

13:02.640 --> 13:03.993
Why are you sorry?

13:05.160 --> 13:07.355
I just find it's easier that way.

13:08.200 --> 13:10.316
Okay. Is Charlie at home?

13:10.480 --> 13:12.869
Oh, no.
He went out a couple of hours ago.

13:13.640 --> 13:16.473
I've been trying to call him on his cell,
but he doesn't answer.

13:16.640 --> 13:19.234
- Well, please tell him I stopped by.
- Sure thing.

13:20.800 --> 13:22.438
Gabrielle?

13:24.320 --> 13:25.753
Forgive me if I'm out of line...

13:25.920 --> 13:31.074
...but I sense a Ioneliness inside you.

13:33.120 --> 13:36.351
- Is it so obvious?
- I'm right?

13:36.520 --> 13:39.273
Oh, yes. But how could you know?

13:40.280 --> 13:41.713
We're two of a kind.

13:41.880 --> 13:47.591
I myself have tasted
the saltiness of Ionely tears.

13:49.560 --> 13:52.472
- We have much to share.
- We do indeed. Come on in.

13:54.320 --> 13:57.437
First his cookies, now his croissant.

14:00.360 --> 14:05.195
Well, in my experience, I've found that
the more beautiful the woman is...

14:05.360 --> 14:06.554
...the Ionelier she is.

14:06.720 --> 14:10.076
That's very true. How do you
know so much about women?

14:10.440 --> 14:12.829
What can I say? I have a knack.

14:15.560 --> 14:18.438
- Hey.
- Oh, hello, Charlie.

14:18.600 --> 14:20.318
Gee, how embarrassing.

14:21.160 --> 14:24.391
- What are you talking about?
- Oh, dear. This is so difficult.

14:24.560 --> 14:26.755
No, it's not. Go ahead, tell him. Tell him.

14:27.320 --> 14:33.316
Charlie, you're a wonderful man, but
your brother, he really understands me.

14:33.960 --> 14:35.439
So, what are you saying?

14:36.800 --> 14:38.392
It's just...

14:38.760 --> 14:40.352
l...

14:41.080 --> 14:44.038
- I can't.
- I can. She's dumping you for me.

14:44.800 --> 14:47.394
This is so awkward. I must go.

14:47.560 --> 14:50.120
Please forgive me?

14:56.080 --> 14:57.195
How does it feel?

14:58.000 --> 15:00.036
- I'm stunned.
- Good, good. What else?

15:00.520 --> 15:02.397
- You snaked my girlfriend?
- Yes, I did.

15:02.560 --> 15:04.869
I snaked her. Like a cobra.

15:06.720 --> 15:10.429
- And you did it just to hurt me?
- Well, not just to hurt you.

15:10.600 --> 15:12.397
Well, yeah, just to hurt you.

15:13.640 --> 15:15.596
I don't know what to say.

15:15.880 --> 15:19.668
- I'm crushed.
- That's good. Say that. "I'm crushed."

15:20.680 --> 15:23.831
My own brother
purposefully set out to hurt me.

15:25.280 --> 15:27.748
Oh, no. Oh, no.
You're not taking this away from me.

15:27.920 --> 15:30.195
What about you
and Charity Kirschenbaum?

15:30.360 --> 15:34.876
I was 17, Alan. I was a horny idiot.
But you, you're an adult.

15:35.040 --> 15:37.918
Okay. I see where you're going,
and it's not gonna work.

15:38.080 --> 15:40.196
You're not taking this away from me.

15:40.360 --> 15:44.035
I really thought our relationship
had grown beyond this petty crap.

15:44.200 --> 15:46.236
I thought I could count on you.

15:46.400 --> 15:47.879
I thought you were my friend.

15:52.600 --> 15:55.034
Son of a bitch. He took it away from me.

16:06.760 --> 16:08.478
Oh, hey. You're here.

16:09.080 --> 16:10.559
Where am I gonna go, Alan?

16:12.680 --> 16:15.752
- You took my girl.
- And I feel awful about that.

16:17.400 --> 16:20.790
- It doesn't matter.
- It does matter. I made a terrible mistake.

16:20.960 --> 16:23.554
I did the worst thing I could possibly do.

16:24.200 --> 16:26.111
I lowered myself to your level.

16:28.000 --> 16:30.275
You know what I mean.
I love you. You're my brother.

16:30.440 --> 16:33.637
- I wouldn't hurt you for the world.
- Actions speak louder than words.

16:33.800 --> 16:36.553
You're right. Okay. Here's an action.

16:40.800 --> 16:42.916
You bought me a bag of cookies.

16:43.080 --> 16:45.275
Sure, that should make up
for stealing Gabrielle.

16:47.640 --> 16:49.995
How about three bags?

16:51.240 --> 16:53.834
And I'm breaking it off with her.
You can have her back.

16:54.000 --> 16:55.558
Have her back?

16:55.720 --> 16:58.393
What is wrong with you?
She's not a lawn mower you borrowed.

16:59.920 --> 17:03.230
You can't just hose off the blades
and give her back.

17:04.280 --> 17:06.919
- But... But...
- "But" nothing.

17:07.080 --> 17:10.516
She dumped me because she likes you.
So, what are you gonna say to her, Alan?

17:10.680 --> 17:14.434
"I was just using you to punish Charlie
for something that happened"?

17:14.600 --> 17:17.433
I probably wouldn't use those words.

17:17.600 --> 17:21.479
You can't ease your conscience
about hurting me by hurting her.

17:21.640 --> 17:24.359
So you're saying
you want me to keep seeing her?

17:24.520 --> 17:27.239
I'm saying
I want you to do the right thing.

17:27.400 --> 17:30.597
- And then you'll forgive me?
- Yes, then I'll forgive you.

17:32.600 --> 17:35.433
Well, okay.

17:35.880 --> 17:40.396
For you,
I'll keep seeing the gorgeous woman.

17:41.600 --> 17:42.589
Thank you.

17:43.680 --> 17:45.272
You're welcome.

17:50.000 --> 17:53.549
- Okay, so, what's the catch?
- Catch?

17:53.880 --> 17:56.314
I don't know what you're talking about.

17:59.000 --> 18:01.833
So are you sure
everything's okay with Charlie?

18:02.000 --> 18:05.549
Everything's great with Charlie.
Charlie's fine. Forget Charlie.

18:08.840 --> 18:10.910
Well, you know, like the song:

18:23.280 --> 18:25.077
Okay.

18:25.800 --> 18:26.789
I'm ready.

18:29.400 --> 18:31.550
- Excuse me?
- Go ahead.

18:31.720 --> 18:33.676
Get it over with.

18:34.360 --> 18:37.477
- I'm not sure I follow.
- Do what you have to do.

18:37.640 --> 18:39.995
Just hurry.

18:40.800 --> 18:43.394
But don't you wanna start
with some kissing...

18:43.560 --> 18:45.790
...and, you know, foreplay?

18:46.320 --> 18:48.197
No, thank you.

18:49.360 --> 18:51.396
How about a smile?

18:55.880 --> 18:57.711
Better?

18:57.880 --> 18:59.916
Actually, worse.

19:00.520 --> 19:03.034
Could you close your eyes again?

19:15.200 --> 19:17.668
- Where are you going?
- I have to brush my teeth.

19:18.120 --> 19:19.348
The bathroom's that way.

19:19.520 --> 19:22.080
Yeah, but my toothbrush is at home.
Bye-bye.

19:32.000 --> 19:34.275
- Hey.
- Hey.

19:34.800 --> 19:36.870
How'd it go with Gabrielle?

19:37.200 --> 19:40.272
- I think you know how it went.
- Yeah, I do.

19:42.080 --> 19:44.196
It's kind of like necrophilia, isn't it?

19:44.360 --> 19:47.113
- I didn't go through with it.
- Really?

19:47.280 --> 19:49.510
I guess we're different that way.

19:51.120 --> 19:55.557
So I didn't really
steal her from you, did I?

19:56.160 --> 19:59.311
- Nope.
- You were trying to get rid of her.

19:59.480 --> 20:04.270
Yep. But I didn't wanna hurt her feelings.
Thanks for helping me out with that.

20:05.360 --> 20:08.432
Well, at least now we're even, right?

20:09.800 --> 20:11.358
- Not quite.
- What do you mean?

20:11.520 --> 20:14.751
Charlie. Coming back to bed?

20:15.240 --> 20:19.791
- Charity? Charity Kirschenbaum?
- Oh, hi, Alan. Long time no see.

20:19.960 --> 20:22.349
Yeah, 20 years.

20:22.520 --> 20:24.795
She looks great, doesn't she?

20:24.960 --> 20:26.632
- Come on, baby.
- But...

20:26.800 --> 20:29.314
Now we're even.

20:35.400 --> 20:41.873
I hate you!

21:05.600 --> 21:07.591
